To maintain strict consistency across engagement modes, BIQ is evaluated across two operational timeframes: • In-Combat Tactical Adaptation (Equal Engagement): Reading an opponent's posture, feinting, adjusting range, and devising immediate countermeasures during an active, unassisted clash. • Pre-Battle Strategic Planning (Situational Engagement): Gathering intelligence, constructing terrain traps, and selecting specialized counter-gear prior to contact. TCC Directive: Elevate Battle Intelligence, spatial control, and tactical execution above raw destructive mass. An unthinking brute with high output remains systematically vulnerable to a disciplined tactician with a viable vector. Pure logic rules here.
