Matchup outcomes frequently depend on how two fighting styles, anatomies, and toolkits interact under pressure: • Asymmetric Archetype Dynamics: A slow, heavy close-quarters bruiser (Tier 5 Striking Force) may effortlessly crush an unarmored melee glass cannon, yet suffer total defeat against an agile ranged tactician (Tier 3) who maintains distance and targets sensory blind spots. • Immunity & Arsenal Counters: Specific biological immunities, environmental adaptations, or specialized equipment can completely neutralize an opponent's primary offensive vector regardless of raw tier classification.
3.	Isolated Encounter Evaluation
Every hypothetical confrontation is modeled independently from first principles: • Direct Parameter Comparison: Analysts compare Combatant A's specific offensive vectors, Combat Speed, BIQ, and Law of Price constraints directly against Combatant B's exact defensive layers and psychological profile. • No Copy-Pasted Profiles: Stats and outcomes are never extrapolated across unrelated fights. Each clash is treated as a unique tactical equation. TCC Directive: Evaluate every matchup as an isolated tactical interaction governed by style compatibility, specific counters, and context—never by transitive ABC victory chains. Pure logic rules here.
TCC Standard Dossier: Operational Baseline vs. Peak-Form Anomalies
