1.	Calibrating Tier 13 (Universal) & Tier 14 (Multiversal)
Within the TCC (The Circular Canon) framework, Tier 13 (Universal) is strictly defined by complete structural creation, reconfiguration, or destruction of a single closed universe or single spacetime continuum. • External Viewpoint Does Not Multiply Scale: Observing a single universe from an external interface, dimensional pocket, or overarching frame does not automatically grant Tier 14 (Multiversal) standing—if the demonstrated impact affects only one universe, the scale remains strictly Tier 13. • Literal Volume Containment: Every isolated simulation or self-contained pocket space is bounded strictly by its demonstrated spatial volume; controlling a microscopic, single-room space holds zero equivalence to restructuring a vast physical cosmos. TCC Directive: Calibrate universal and multiversal tiers strictly by the literal structural scope affected rather than external vantage points. Pure logic rules here.
